.IX Title "Lucy::Simple 3pm"
.TH Lucy::Simple 3pm 2026-09-16 "perl v5.40.1" "User Contributed Perl Documentation"
.\" For nroff, turn off justification.  Always turn off hyphenation; it makes
.\" way too many mistakes in technical documents.
.if n .ad l
.nh
.SH NAME
Lucy::Simple \- Basic search engine.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.IX Header "SYNOPSIS"
First, build an index of your documents.
.PP
.Vb 4
\&    my $index = Lucy::Simple\->new(
\&        path     => \*(Aq/path/to/index/\*(Aq
\&        language => \*(Aqen\*(Aq,
\&    );
\&
\&    while ( my ( $title, $content ) = each %source_docs ) {
\&        $index\->add_doc({
\&            title    => $title,
\&            content  => $content,
\&        });
\&    }
.Ve
.PP
Later, search the index.
.PP
.Vb 5
\&    my $total_hits = $index\->search(
\&        query      => $query_string,
\&        offset     => 0,
\&        num_wanted => 10,
\&    );
\&
\&    print "Total hits: $total_hits\en";
\&    while ( my $hit = $index\->next ) {
\&        print "$hit\->{title}\en",
\&    }
.Ve
.SH DESCRIPTION
.IX Header "DESCRIPTION"
Lucy::Simple is a stripped-down interface for the Lucy search
engine library.
.SH CONSTRUCTORS
.IX Header "CONSTRUCTORS"
.SS new
.IX Subsection "new"
.Vb 4
\&    my $lucy = Lucy::Simple\->new(
\&        path     => \*(Aq/path/to/index/\*(Aq,
\&        language => \*(Aqen\*(Aq,
\&    );
.Ve
.PP
Create a Lucy::Simple object, which can be used for both indexing and
searching.  Both parameters \f(CW\*(C`path\*(C'\fR and \f(CW\*(C`language\*(C'\fR are required.
.IP \(bu 4
\&\fBpath\fR \- Where the index directory should be located.  If no index
is found at the specified location, one will be created.
.IP \(bu 4
\&\fBlanguage\fR \- The language of the documents in your collection,
indicated  by a two-letter ISO code.  12 languages are supported:
.Sp
.Vb 10
\&    |\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-|
\&    | Language   | ISO code |
\&    |\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-|
\&    | Danish     | da       |
\&    | Dutch      | nl       |
\&    | English    | en       |
\&    | Finnish    | fi       |
\&    | French     | fr       |
\&    | German     | de       |
\&    | Italian    | it       |
\&    | Norwegian  | no       |
\&    | Portuguese | pt       |
\&    | Spanish    | es       |
\&    | Swedish    | sv       |
\&    | Russian    | ru       |
\&    |\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-|
.Ve
.SH METHODS
.IX Header "METHODS"
.SS add_doc
.IX Subsection "add_doc"
.Vb 5
\&    $lucy\->add_doc({
\&        location => $url,
\&        title    => $title,
\&        content  => $content,
\&    });
.Ve
.PP
Add a document to the index. The document must be supplied as a hashref,
with field names as keys and content as values.
.SS search
.IX Subsection "search"
.Vb 6
\&    my $int = $simple\->search(
\&        query      => $query,       # required
\&        offset     => $offset,      # default: 0
\&        num_wanted => $num_wanted,  # default: 10
\&        sort_spec  => $sort_spec,   # default: undef
\&    );
.Ve
.PP
Search the index.  Returns the total number of documents which match
the query.  (This number is unlikely to match \f(CW\*(C`num_wanted\*(C'\fR.)
.IP \(bu 4
\&\fBquery\fR \- A search query string.
.IP \(bu 4
\&\fBoffset\fR \- The number of most-relevant hits to discard, typically
used when “paging” through hits N at a time.  Setting offset to 20 and
num_wanted to 10 retrieves hits 21\-30, assuming that 30 hits can be
found.
.IP \(bu 4
\&\fBnum_wanted\fR \- The number of hits you would like to see after
\&\f(CW\*(C`offset\*(C'\fR is taken into account.
.IP \(bu 4
\&\fBsort_spec\fR \- A SortSpec, which will affect how results are
ranked and returned.
.SS next
.IX Subsection "next"
.Vb 1
\&    my $hit_doc = $simple\->next();
.Ve
.PP
Return the next hit, or undef when the iterator is exhausted.
.SH INHERITANCE
.IX Header "INHERITANCE"
Lucy::Simple isa Clownfish::Obj.
